WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:05.460
Captain's Log, Stardate 50537.2.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.973
Routine scans
of an uninhabited star system

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.542
have revealed the presence
of gallicite,

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.273
a very rare substance,
on the fourth planet.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.247
If these readings are right,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.841
we're looking at a yield
of nearly a kiloton.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.784
That would be enough gallicite

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.980
to completely refit
the warp coils.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.320
They sure could use it
with all the damage

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.154
they've taken
the past two years.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.318
Is there anyone in the area

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.884
who might consider this
their property?

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.122
There are indications

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.688
that a colony once existed
on the planet's surface.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.996
However, it appears
to be long abandoned.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.503
All right,
let's stake a claim.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.835
I'll leave this
in your hands, B'Elanna.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.841
Use whatever resources
and personnel you need.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.103
You might want to talk
to Mr. Neelix.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.008
I believe he spent some time
working in a mining colony.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.569
Aye, Captain.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.181
These tunnels are
clearly artificial.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.616
Someone else must've
been interested

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.778
in digging up this gallicite.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.288
That should make it easier
to access the deposits.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.789
True, but we have to be careful.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.122
There's been a lot of
seismic activity down there.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.287
Look, these tunnels
are completely collapsed.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.762
We should bring Tom Paris
on the away team.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.562
He's had quite a lot
of rock-climbing experience.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.467
I have spent several summers
exploring the Osana caverns,

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.971
which involved
some quite treacherous climbing.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.200
Great. You two can be
our safety experts.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.170
Have we completed
our preparations

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.841
to your satisfaction?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.975
We're done here, yes.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:29.148
Let me take this opportunity
to declare Koon-ut so'lik...

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.555
my desire to become your mate.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.559
What?

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.118
In human terms, I am...

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.754
proposing marriage.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.162
Do you accept?

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.861
Uh, this is a-a little sudden...

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.334
isn't it?

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.532
Besides, I thought that
Vulcan marriages were arranged.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:49.007
Don't you already have somebody
back home?

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.602
She has sufficient reason
to consider me lost,

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.010
and has most likely chosen
another mate.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.447
It's appropriate for me
to do the same.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.951
And you've chosen me.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.452
I've come to greatly admire

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.614
not only your impressive
technical skills,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.953
but also your bravery
and sense of moral duty...

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.289
all excellent qualities
in a prospective mate.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.885
But you're a Vulcan.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.623
I am... half Klingon.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.961
I really can't imagine...

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.900
Perhaps we are not
an obvious match.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.835
However, our differences
would complement each other.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.964
You've often expressed
frustration

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.405
with your Klingon temper.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.466
My mental discipline
would help you control it.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.477
Furthermore, I feel that...

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.637
Wait, please.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.077
Please. Um...

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:30.810
I see that you've given this
a lot of, um, logical thought,

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.978
and, uh, I really am
very flattered...

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.318
but my answer is no.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.355
I'm sorry.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.223
B'Elanna...

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.787
you may wish to reconsider.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.299
Your choices for a mate
are currently limited

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.096
to 73 male crew members
on this ship...

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.830
some of whom are
already unavailable.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.770
I'll worry about my choices
myself, thank you.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.330
I should also remind you
that many humanoid species

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.843
are unable to withstand
Klingon mating practices.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.003
Okay, that's enough.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.478
Whereas, my superior
Vulcan strength

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.980
would make me
a very suitable partner.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:09.435
Here are the results
of his cortical scan.

00:05:09.474 --> 00:05:11.840
So, what's wrong with him?

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.710
In addition to a dislocated jaw,

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:17.306
Ensign Vorik seems
to be suffering

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:18.941
from a neurochemical imbalance.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.952
Meaning... what?

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:26.851
I believe I should discuss that
with the patient privately.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:36.429
You're going through
the Pon farr, aren't you?

00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:41.762
That's an extremely...

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.468
personal question, Doctor.

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:45.135
Yes, I'm aware
that Vulcans prefer

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:48.203
to keep their mating practices
very much to themselves.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.976
There's almost nothing
in the medical database

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.778
beyond a few observations
made by Starfleet doctors

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.217
over the years.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.413
Your symptoms...

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.979
the chemical imbalance and
loss of emotional control...

00:05:58.056 --> 00:05:59.990
are consistent
with those observations.

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:02.357
Have you been eating
and sleeping normally?

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:04.726
I knew there was
something wrong.

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.594
I was hoping it wasn't...

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.792
this.

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.495
I assume this is
your first Pon farr?

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.934
There's nothing
to be embarrassed about.

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:15.940
It's a normal
biological function.

00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:17.601
I'll do what I can
to help you through it,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.702
but I'll need
a little more information.

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:22.714
We do not discuss it.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.375
I'm afraid you'll have to.

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:26.543
You have a severe imbalance
in your brain chemistry.

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:29.145
If it gets much worse, it could
become life-threatening.

00:06:29.187 --> 00:06:31.985
Now I need to know how Vulcans
deal with this condition.

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:42.623
We...

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.193
go home.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.967
Every seven years
of our adult life,

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:51.305
Vulcans experience
an instinctual...

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:54.835
irresistible urge
to return to the homeworld

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.940
and... take a mate.

00:06:57.983 --> 00:07:01.612
But in your case, being stranded

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:04.588
halfway across the galaxy,
that's impossible.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:05.647
Yes.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.023
So, then, logically,
you try to find a mate here.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.618
I assume that explains
your behavior

00:07:09.661 --> 00:07:10.889
toward Lieutenant Torres.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:14.023
I have always had great
respect for B'Elanna.

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.193
I hope she isn't too...

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:17.565
upset with me.

00:07:17.602 --> 00:07:21.402
With Lieutenant Torres,
"upset" is a relative term.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.340
In any case, we're going
to have to try to find

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:26.503
another way to treat
your condition.

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:27.910
Let's start with
a micro-cellular scan.

00:07:27.946 --> 00:07:29.106
No!

00:07:30.115 --> 00:07:32.777
I don't want medical treatment.

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:34.809
I will resolve this myself.

00:07:34.853 --> 00:07:37.117
How do you intend to do that?

00:07:37.155 --> 00:07:39.953
There are certain
meditative techniques.

00:07:40.025 --> 00:07:42.858
I will be fine
if simply left alone.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:44.293
Please...

00:07:44.329 --> 00:07:45.762
allow me to return
to my quarters.

00:07:45.797 --> 00:07:47.321
Confine me there if you wish,

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.995
but allow me to resolve
my situation privately.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:56.898
Until I have a better idea

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:58.910
of how to treat
your condition...

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:00.844
I'll release you
to your quarters.

00:08:02.814 --> 00:08:04.179
You'll be under confinement

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:08.516
and wearing a cortical
monitor at all times.

00:08:12.924 --> 00:08:14.687
Thank you.

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:24.463
I'm concerned about Ensign
Vorik's cortical readings.

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:26.095
One returns to normal levels.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:27.571
Then another one spikes.

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:28.868
It's chaotic, as if the brain's

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:31.068
regulatory system
had simply shut down.

00:08:31.109 --> 00:08:33.475
I can't tell if he's
making any progress

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.207
with these meditations.

00:08:35.247 --> 00:08:36.714
I thought maybe
you could suggest

00:08:36.748 --> 00:08:38.477
other possible treatments.

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:39.950
I cannot.

00:08:40.018 --> 00:08:41.645
Is that because you don't know

00:08:41.686 --> 00:08:43.085
or because you don't want
to discuss it?

00:08:43.121 --> 00:08:44.918
For both of those reasons,

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:46.617
there is little help
that I can offer.

00:08:46.658 --> 00:08:48.956
It is inappropriate
for me to involve myself

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:50.757
in Ensign Vorik's
personal situation.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.264
For such an intellectually
enlightened race,

00:08:53.298 --> 00:08:56.961
Vulcans have a remarkably
Victorian attitude about sex.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.970
That is a very human
judgment, Doctor.

00:09:00.005 --> 00:09:01.302
Then here's a Vulcan one.

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:04.502
I fail to see the logic
in perpetuating ignorance

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:06.738
about a basic
biological function.

00:09:06.778 --> 00:09:10.214
There is nothing logical
about the Pon farr.

00:09:10.248 --> 00:09:12.910
It is a time
when instinct and emotion

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:14.508
dominate over reason.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:17.522
It cannot be analyzed
by the rational mind

00:09:17.556 --> 00:09:20.081
nor cured by
conventional medicine.

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:21.387
Anyone who has experienced it

00:09:21.426 --> 00:09:23.394
understands that it
must simply be followed

00:09:23.428 --> 00:09:24.690
to its natural resolution.

00:09:24.729 --> 00:09:27.357
Which is what, exactly?

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.765
There are three options
that I am aware of:

00:09:31.803 --> 00:09:35.933
Taking a mate, which Ensign
Vorik has already attempted;

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:38.807
the ritual combat,
which does not apply

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.072
to his situation.

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.602
Combat?

00:09:41.646 --> 00:09:43.807
An ancient tradition
of fighting for one's mate...

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:46.909
which, as I have said,
is not relevant here.

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:50.285
The third alternative
is the intensive meditation

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:51.653
he has chosen to try.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.420
Isn't there anything we can do
to help him with that?

00:09:54.459 --> 00:09:56.324
I believe that any interference

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:58.795
would be unwelcome
and counterproductive.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.628
You must allow him to face
this challenge privately.

00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:03.600
If he possesses
enough discipline

00:10:03.635 --> 00:10:06.468
to reach a point
of psychological resolution,

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:08.837
then his chemical imbalance
should correct itself.

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:12.640
The Vulcan brain
never ceases to amaze me.

00:10:12.677 --> 00:10:16.238
Thank you, Lieutenant.
You've been a great help.

00:10:23.054 --> 00:10:25.181
Ah, you two are awfully prompt.

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:26.884
Impressed?

00:10:26.925 --> 00:10:28.222
Oh, it'll take
a little more work

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.693
than that to impress me,
Lieutenant.

00:10:29.728 --> 00:10:31.992
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:32.063 --> 00:10:36.466
All right. Let me show you
our target area.

00:10:36.501 --> 00:10:38.469
Shouldn't we wait
for Ensign Vorik?

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:39.595
He's not coming.

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:40.696
This seems to be

00:10:40.739 --> 00:10:42.229
the most accessible vein
of gallicite.

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:43.241
We'll beam to the surface

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:44.503
then go down
through this passageway

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:46.010
until it dead-ends
in this chamber.

00:10:46.111 --> 00:10:49.012
Then we'll descend almost
50 meters, almost straight down.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.843
Do you see any problem
with that, Tom?

00:10:50.882 --> 00:10:52.543
Um... well, as long

00:10:52.584 --> 00:10:55.917
as we go slow and easy,
we'll be fine.

00:10:55.954 --> 00:10:57.012
Good.
You're all set, Neelix?

00:10:57.088 --> 00:10:58.953
I've got a laser drill,
sample cases,

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.321
geo-spectral analysis kit...

00:11:00.358 --> 00:11:01.347
In other words, you're ready.

00:11:01.393 --> 00:11:02.382
Let's go.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.664
This way.

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:17.902
Look over here.

00:11:19.611 --> 00:11:21.977
This must have been the colony.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.447
Not more than 50
or 60 years ago...

00:11:25.483 --> 00:11:27.417
hardly enough time
for these structures

00:11:27.452 --> 00:11:29.215
to decay so badly.

00:11:29.254 --> 00:11:32.189
They must have suffered
some kind of disaster...

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:33.486
maybe an earthquake.

00:11:33.525 --> 00:11:35.322
Well, we'll send down an
archaeological team later on.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.725
Right now, we've got
our own work to do.

00:11:36.761 --> 00:11:37.989
Are we in a rush?

00:11:38.063 --> 00:11:40.588
I just don't see any point
in wasting time...

00:11:40.632 --> 00:11:43.430
unless, of course,
you want to stall,

00:11:43.468 --> 00:11:46.733
to put off demonstrating
your climbing expertise.

00:11:47.906 --> 00:11:49.771
Grab your gear
and try to keep up.

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:08.485
No matter how real
a holodeck program may seem,

00:12:08.526 --> 00:12:10.255
it just doesn't get
your heart pumping

00:12:10.295 --> 00:12:11.853
like a genuine
physical challenge.

00:12:11.896 --> 00:12:12.885
It's exhilarating.

00:12:16.835 --> 00:12:18.962
If you're looking
for exhilaration...

00:12:21.473 --> 00:12:24.909
It didn't look quite so steep
on the sensor map, did it?

00:12:24.943 --> 00:12:26.672
We're prepared for this.

00:12:26.711 --> 00:12:27.973
We can handle it.

00:12:28.046 --> 00:12:29.707
Let's go.

00:12:34.185 --> 00:12:37.951
All this Starfleet technology
almost takes the fun out of it.

00:12:37.989 --> 00:12:41.186
If you mean the fun of wondering
whether your anchor will hold

00:12:41.226 --> 00:12:44.753
while you're dangling over
a cliff, I think I'll pass.

00:12:44.796 --> 00:12:46.525
See you below.

00:12:54.539 --> 00:12:57.531
You go first.
I'll follow you.

00:13:11.722 --> 00:13:13.485
Watch your footing!

00:13:14.558 --> 00:13:15.525
You're right.

00:13:15.559 --> 00:13:17.083
My heart is pumping faster.

00:13:17.127 --> 00:13:19.925
Wait till we climb back up
with a pack full of gallicite.

00:13:19.963 --> 00:13:22.261
Oh, I'm just getting warmed up.

00:13:28.638 --> 00:13:30.367
No!

00:13:45.856 --> 00:13:47.118
Are you hurt?

00:13:47.157 --> 00:13:49.990
You, you almost
got us both killed!

00:13:50.093 --> 00:13:51.856
I'm sorry.

00:13:51.895 --> 00:13:53.362
I don't know what happened.

00:13:54.531 --> 00:13:56.294
Careful, careful.

00:13:56.333 --> 00:13:57.664
You might have broken it.

00:13:57.701 --> 00:14:00.693
You had no business
rigging safety equipment

00:14:00.737 --> 00:14:02.796
when you had no idea
what you were doing!

00:14:02.839 --> 00:14:03.931
Calm down.

00:14:04.007 --> 00:14:05.372
This wasn't Neelix's fault.

00:14:05.409 --> 00:14:07.809
I saw him drive the piton,
and it was solid.

00:14:07.844 --> 00:14:09.311
It must have malfunctioned.

00:14:09.346 --> 00:14:10.472
You are hurt.

00:14:10.514 --> 00:14:12.175
I'm fine.
No thanks to you two.

00:14:12.215 --> 00:14:14.513
I would have been better
coming down here alone.

00:14:14.551 --> 00:14:16.212
Don't you think you're
overreacting a little bit?

00:14:16.253 --> 00:14:17.811
Just drag him to the ship.

00:14:17.854 --> 00:14:18.946
I'll get the gallicite myself.

00:14:19.022 --> 00:14:21.047
We can't leave you
down here alone.

00:14:21.091 --> 00:14:22.388
He's right.

00:14:22.426 --> 00:14:24.360
Let's contact the ship.

00:14:24.394 --> 00:14:26.157
You get your hands off of me.

00:14:28.298 --> 00:14:29.265
B'Elanna!

00:14:29.299 --> 00:14:31.597
What is wrong with you?

00:14:32.936 --> 00:14:33.960
Nothing.

00:14:34.071 --> 00:14:36.437
I'm in charge of this mission.

00:14:36.473 --> 00:14:38.134
I'll finish it.

00:14:39.142 --> 00:14:40.575
Wait.

00:14:41.912 --> 00:14:43.402
Go ahead, Tom.

00:14:43.447 --> 00:14:45.210
I'll be all right here.

00:14:47.918 --> 00:14:48.976
The last thing we need

00:14:49.086 --> 00:14:50.883
is for all three of us
to split up.

00:14:50.921 --> 00:14:52.582
Paris to Voyager.

00:14:52.622 --> 00:14:54.681
We've got problems down here.

00:14:58.495 --> 00:15:00.463
I haven't been able
to contact her.

00:15:00.497 --> 00:15:02.522
She's either
out of communications range

00:15:02.566 --> 00:15:03.658
or just not responding.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:04.826
Where is she now?

00:15:04.868 --> 00:15:06.028
The last location

00:15:06.069 --> 00:15:08.663
I can verify
is about ten meters below us.

00:15:08.705 --> 00:15:10.673
I tried to stop her
from leaving, Captain,

00:15:10.707 --> 00:15:14.404
but she got very hostile
and... bit me.

00:15:15.445 --> 00:15:17.413
She bit you?

00:15:17.447 --> 00:15:21.076
And she seemed to be enjoying it
in a Klingon kind of way.

00:15:21.118 --> 00:15:22.745
She's really not herself.

00:15:29.326 --> 00:15:32.352
Any luck in getting
a transporter lock on them?

00:15:32.395 --> 00:15:34.625
No. They're too far
beneath the surface.

00:15:34.664 --> 00:15:36.461
Tom, I'm sending an away team
down to you.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.593
We'll get Neelix out of there,
then go after B'Elanna.

00:15:38.635 --> 00:15:40.125
Tuvok, you're with Chakotay.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.661
Captain, I'd like to request
a short delay.

00:15:42.706 --> 00:15:46.107
I may have an explanation
for Lieutenant Torres' behavior.

00:15:51.047 --> 00:15:52.412
Go away.

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:55.943
I said...

00:15:55.986 --> 00:15:57.078
go away!

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:00.112
I'm sorry, sir.

00:16:00.157 --> 00:16:04.526
No. I must apologize
for the intrusion,

00:16:04.561 --> 00:16:07.826
particularly at this time.

00:16:07.864 --> 00:16:09.627
Then you know.

00:16:09.666 --> 00:16:11.600
Yes. I regret

00:16:11.635 --> 00:16:14.263
that I must ask you some
uncomfortable questions

00:16:14.304 --> 00:16:15.862
regarding Lieutenant Torres.

00:16:15.906 --> 00:16:18.136
Yes, sir.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.936
It is important for me
to know specifically

00:16:23.013 --> 00:16:25.675
what happened between
the two of you.

00:16:25.715 --> 00:16:28.445
Was there any physical contact?

00:16:28.485 --> 00:16:30.953
Yes.

00:16:30.987 --> 00:16:34.013
Please describe your actions.

00:16:35.926 --> 00:16:38.156
It's... hard to remember.

00:16:38.195 --> 00:16:40.561
I was acting irrationally.

00:16:41.798 --> 00:16:45.234
I believe... I approached her.

00:16:51.575 --> 00:16:52.837
I...

00:16:54.344 --> 00:16:55.868
I touched her face.

00:16:55.912 --> 00:16:57.846
I meant to be gentle,

00:16:57.881 --> 00:16:59.974
but she tried to move away

00:17:00.016 --> 00:17:02.883
and then I was
holding her more tightly,

00:17:02.919 --> 00:17:05.854
both hands on her face,
like this.

00:17:05.889 --> 00:17:09.916
It felt very important
not to let go.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.394
I'm... I'm not certain why.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:18.160
I believe you were initiating
a telepathic mating bond.

00:17:18.201 --> 00:17:21.796
I... didn't know
it could happen that way.

00:17:21.838 --> 00:17:28.573
I wanted to bond with her.
That much I remember clearly.

00:17:28.612 --> 00:17:30.170
Apparently, you succeeded.

00:17:30.213 --> 00:17:33.080
Lieutenant Torres has been
displaying unusual behavior,

00:17:33.116 --> 00:17:36.916
very much like
the early stages of Pon farr.

00:17:40.557 --> 00:17:41.615
How is that possible?

00:17:41.658 --> 00:17:43.717
She's not Vulcan.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:44.886
There have been instances

00:17:44.928 --> 00:17:47.863
of Vulcans mating
with members of other races.

00:17:49.399 --> 00:17:52.527
But she rejected me, forcefully.

00:17:52.569 --> 00:17:54.264
Even a brief moment of bonding

00:17:54.304 --> 00:17:56.431
may have been enough
to disrupt her self-control,

00:17:56.473 --> 00:17:59.533
as the Pon farr does in us.

00:17:59.576 --> 00:18:03.137
In a half-Klingon, the effects
may be even more extreme.

00:18:03.179 --> 00:18:05.340
I have to go to her.

00:18:05.382 --> 00:18:07.282
You cannot.

00:18:07.317 --> 00:18:10.150
Lieutenant Torres is out
of contact on the planet.

00:18:10.186 --> 00:18:11.915
Then I'll find her.

00:18:12.022 --> 00:18:14.456
B'Elanna needs me,
and I need her.

00:18:14.491 --> 00:18:16.789
It is a far more
sensible strategy

00:18:16.826 --> 00:18:18.851
to get her safely
back to Voyager

00:18:18.895 --> 00:18:21.159
and then decide on
the proper resolution.

00:18:21.197 --> 00:18:23.461
The resolution must be
that we become mates.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.092
It is only logical.

00:18:25.135 --> 00:18:29.231
Lieutenant Torres has never been
a great follower of logic.

00:18:29.272 --> 00:18:32.298
You think
she'll reject me again?

00:18:32.342 --> 00:18:34.674
It might be wise

00:18:34.711 --> 00:18:37.202
to continue
your meditative efforts.

00:18:40.984 --> 00:18:43.043
I'll do my best, sir.

00:18:51.961 --> 00:18:53.929
It is difficult to estimate
how soon her condition

00:18:53.963 --> 00:18:55.123
will become life-threatening.

00:18:55.165 --> 00:18:57.258
Life-threatening?
She could die from this?

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:58.267
Yes.

00:18:58.301 --> 00:18:59.928
And you've gone through it

00:18:59.969 --> 00:19:02.096
every seven years
of your adult life?

00:19:02.138 --> 00:19:03.730
You only need to be concerned

00:19:03.773 --> 00:19:06.105
with Lieutenant Torres'
situation.

00:19:06.142 --> 00:19:08.508
Right.

00:19:08.545 --> 00:19:11.343
Well, it looks like
finding her won't be easy.

00:19:11.381 --> 00:19:13.246
Scanning range is limited
to about 20 meters,

00:19:13.283 --> 00:19:15.444
and even that's
not too reliable.

00:19:15.485 --> 00:19:17.419
You said she was
going after the gallicite,

00:19:17.454 --> 00:19:19.547
so we'll do the same,
and hope it leads us to her.

00:19:19.589 --> 00:19:21.420
I'm ready to go, Commander.

00:19:38.441 --> 00:19:39.703
Let's go.

00:20:40.837 --> 00:20:42.566
B'Elanna.

00:20:42.605 --> 00:20:44.505
Tom.

00:20:44.541 --> 00:20:46.304
Come here,
you've got to see this.

00:20:46.342 --> 00:20:47.809
How are you feeling,
Lieutenant?

00:20:47.844 --> 00:20:50.005
Fine. This is
an active power system.

00:20:50.046 --> 00:20:51.707
It must have been built
by the colonists.

00:20:51.748 --> 00:20:53.511
We'll send somebody
down here to study it

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:54.676
more closely.

00:20:54.717 --> 00:20:56.651
Right now, we've got to get you
back to the ship.

00:20:56.686 --> 00:20:59.621
No. No. This is my discovery.
It's my mission.

00:20:59.656 --> 00:21:01.749
You don't understand.

00:21:01.791 --> 00:21:04.521
This is the source
of the gallicite readings.

00:21:04.561 --> 00:21:06.756
These conduits are covered
with gallicite plating.

00:21:06.796 --> 00:21:08.297
It's exactly what we need,
and I found it.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.397
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:21:09.431 --> 00:21:11.695
You've succeeded
in your mission.

00:21:11.733 --> 00:21:13.598
Now you must tend to yourself.

00:21:13.635 --> 00:21:16.570
You're experiencing
a condition known as Pon farr.

00:21:18.573 --> 00:21:19.904
Pon what?

00:21:19.941 --> 00:21:21.738
Your emotional balance
has been disrupted.

00:21:21.777 --> 00:21:23.301
You may not be in control

00:21:23.345 --> 00:21:25.245
of your more aggressive
instincts.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:29.910
I lost my temper for a minute.
That's all.

00:21:33.055 --> 00:21:36.491
Why are you all
staring at me like that?

00:21:36.525 --> 00:21:38.993
Please, come back
with us to the ship.

00:21:39.061 --> 00:21:40.858
Just leave me alone.

00:21:58.447 --> 00:22:00.005
Who are you?

00:22:00.082 --> 00:22:01.242
What do you want?

00:22:01.283 --> 00:22:02.875
My name is Chakotay.

00:22:02.918 --> 00:22:04.943
I assure you we have
no hostile intent.

00:22:05.053 --> 00:22:06.520
She does.

00:22:06.555 --> 00:22:07.783
B'Elanna, please.

00:22:07.823 --> 00:22:09.381
She is suffering
from a chemical imbalance

00:22:09.424 --> 00:22:11.255
which is affecting her behavior.

00:22:11.293 --> 00:22:12.521
An imbalance?

00:22:12.561 --> 00:22:13.789
Is it contagious?

00:22:13.829 --> 00:22:17.060
No. However, she does
need our assistance.

00:22:17.099 --> 00:22:19.624
We'd be glad to take her
and leave your territory.

00:22:19.668 --> 00:22:22.068
Not before you tell me
why you came here.

00:22:22.104 --> 00:22:23.833
We only came to find
some gallicite.

00:22:23.872 --> 00:22:26.340
We thought this planet
was uninhabited.

00:22:26.375 --> 00:22:28.206
Then why are you
carrying weapons?

00:22:28.243 --> 00:22:30.074
It's standard procedure
for any mission

00:22:30.112 --> 00:22:31.409
into unfamiliar territory.

00:22:32.881 --> 00:22:34.246
Let me see one.

00:22:45.193 --> 00:22:46.387
And what is that?

00:22:46.428 --> 00:22:48.623
Some sort of scanning device?

00:22:48.663 --> 00:22:50.187
Yes. It's called a tricorder.

00:22:50.232 --> 00:22:53.360
But it didn't detect
any life-forms here?

00:22:53.402 --> 00:22:54.835
No, it didn't.

00:23:00.642 --> 00:23:01.609
What's that?

00:23:01.643 --> 00:23:03.406
Seismic alert.

00:23:03.445 --> 00:23:05.640
That wall is unstable.

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:07.147
Be careful.

00:23:12.954 --> 00:23:14.421
Watch out.

00:23:22.831 --> 00:23:25.095
B'Elanna, don't!

00:23:31.907 --> 00:23:34.034
B'Elanna!

00:23:59.234 --> 00:24:02.795
There must be a hidden door,
some kind of a passageway.

00:24:02.838 --> 00:24:04.931
I'm not picking up anything
like that...

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:08.407
or any life signs.

00:24:08.443 --> 00:24:10.104
Then you're using it wrong.

00:24:10.145 --> 00:24:12.340
Yeah, that must be it...

00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:14.712
or else these aliens
are generating

00:24:14.749 --> 00:24:17.013
some kind of interference
so we can't detect them.

00:24:20.055 --> 00:24:23.047
We have to get out of here
before they come back.

00:24:23.091 --> 00:24:25.184
We can't leave
Chakotay and Tuvok.

00:24:25.227 --> 00:24:28.424
If you have any ideas how
to find them, I'm listening.

00:24:36.438 --> 00:24:40.067
We have to get back to the ship
and get some help...

00:24:40.108 --> 00:24:42.269
for them and for you.

00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:46.371
Why does everybody keep saying
there's something wrong with me?

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:50.616
I'll try to explain it to you.

00:24:50.652 --> 00:24:52.677
But we've got to get moving.

00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:02.927
There.

00:25:03.031 --> 00:25:05.932
Your serotonin levels
are stabilized for the moment,

00:25:05.967 --> 00:25:08.663
but I'm concerned
about these fluctuations.

00:25:08.703 --> 00:25:11.137
It's becoming more difficult
to compensate.

00:25:11.172 --> 00:25:13.367
I will increase my efforts...

00:25:13.408 --> 00:25:15.171
to control them, Doctor.

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:17.405
I'd like you to consider
an alternative treatment

00:25:17.445 --> 00:25:18.412
I've been developing.

00:25:18.446 --> 00:25:20.778
No, I will deal
with this myself.

00:25:20.815 --> 00:25:22.942
Ensign, your life is at risk.

00:25:22.984 --> 00:25:25.214
You don't understand.

00:25:25.253 --> 00:25:27.084
How well a Vulcan copes

00:25:27.122 --> 00:25:29.955
with this experience
is a test of his character.

00:25:30.058 --> 00:25:33.960
I've already humiliated
myself and Lieutenant Tuvok

00:25:33.995 --> 00:25:37.829
by allowing a private matter
to become so...

00:25:37.866 --> 00:25:39.458
public.

00:25:40.669 --> 00:25:43.160
Give yourself a little credit.

00:25:43.204 --> 00:25:44.671
You're doing the best you can

00:25:44.706 --> 00:25:47.300
under unusually
difficult circumstances.

00:25:47.342 --> 00:25:48.707
If you were back on Vulcan,

00:25:48.743 --> 00:25:50.973
you'd have your family and
friends there to help you.

00:25:51.046 --> 00:25:53.879
I shouldn't need any help.

00:25:53.915 --> 00:25:56.975
I know that self-sufficiency
is very important to a Vulcan,

00:25:57.052 --> 00:25:59.486
but there is nothing
shameful in getting

00:25:59.521 --> 00:26:01.921
a little guidance
every once in a while.

00:26:01.990 --> 00:26:05.221
I'd like you to consider
my alternative,

00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:08.559
and then you can decide
whether or not to try it.

00:26:12.167 --> 00:26:13.600
Ensign.

00:26:16.538 --> 00:26:19.405
I don't understand
the purpose of coming here.

00:26:19.441 --> 00:26:20.601
Trust me.

00:26:20.642 --> 00:26:21.609
Ensign Vorik,

00:26:21.643 --> 00:26:24.111
I'd like you to meet T'Pera.

00:26:24.145 --> 00:26:28.809
Surely you're not suggesting
that she become my mate.

00:26:28.850 --> 00:26:33.082
Well, I wouldn't recommend
a lifetime commitment, but...

00:26:33.121 --> 00:26:36.921
she might be able to help you
with your immediate problem.

00:26:40.395 --> 00:26:42.522
She's a hologram.

00:26:42.564 --> 00:26:44.191
She isn't real.

00:26:44.232 --> 00:26:46.564
Then I assume you have
the same low regard for me.

00:26:46.601 --> 00:26:48.660
You're a skilled physician,
Doctor,

00:26:48.703 --> 00:26:50.864
but let me point out
the limitations

00:26:50.905 --> 00:26:53.703
to your own experience
with physical matters.

00:26:53.742 --> 00:26:55.369
I believe we're discussing

00:26:55.410 --> 00:26:57.844
your sexual difficulties
at the moment, Ensign.

00:26:57.879 --> 00:26:59.073
And this holographic mate

00:26:59.114 --> 00:27:00.479
is the best solution
I can think of.

00:27:00.515 --> 00:27:02.915
She won't be the same
as a real mate.

00:27:03.018 --> 00:27:05.509
The difference is
all in your mind,

00:27:05.553 --> 00:27:08.181
which, if I've understood you
and Mr. Tuvok correctly,

00:27:08.223 --> 00:27:11.249
is where the Pon farr
must ultimately be resolved.

00:27:11.292 --> 00:27:15.160
Let your mind convince your body
that she...

00:27:15.196 --> 00:27:19.030
is exactly what you
need her to be.

00:27:19.067 --> 00:27:22.798
Think of this as an advanced
self-healing technique.

00:27:22.837 --> 00:27:24.270
It will still require
considerable

00:27:24.305 --> 00:27:26.603
mental discipline on your part.

00:27:26.641 --> 00:27:32.375
There is a certain logic
to your suggestion, Doctor.

00:27:33.882 --> 00:27:35.179
I will try.

00:27:35.216 --> 00:27:36.808
Good.

00:27:39.654 --> 00:27:43.454
Well, then, I'll leave
the two of you alone.

00:27:50.632 --> 00:27:52.725
Tuvok must be wrong
about this Pon farr business.

00:27:52.767 --> 00:27:53.927
It doesn't make any sense.

00:27:53.968 --> 00:27:55.765
It does explain
how you've been acting.

00:27:55.804 --> 00:27:57.897
I don't see what's so strange.

00:27:57.939 --> 00:28:01.204
How about starting a fight
with a group of armed aliens?

00:28:01.242 --> 00:28:03.301
Shouting at Neelix?
Giving me this?

00:28:03.344 --> 00:28:05.812
If I remember
my Klingon customs,

00:28:05.847 --> 00:28:07.906
biting someone
on the face means...

00:28:08.016 --> 00:28:10.280
I know what it means.

00:28:15.056 --> 00:28:16.683
All right.

00:28:16.725 --> 00:28:18.852
So, maybe I do feel...

00:28:18.893 --> 00:28:21.259
something, some kind of...

00:28:21.296 --> 00:28:23.355
instinct.

00:28:23.398 --> 00:28:25.195
What am I supposed
to do about it?

00:28:30.205 --> 00:28:32.366
When we get back to the ship,

00:28:32.407 --> 00:28:34.705
the Doctor should
be able to help...

00:28:34.743 --> 00:28:36.677
or there's always Vorik.

00:28:36.711 --> 00:28:40.306
I am not helping
that Vulcan pahtk.

00:28:40.348 --> 00:28:41.583
The idea of bonding with him...

00:28:41.583 --> 00:28:43.210
The idea of bonding with him...

00:28:43.251 --> 00:28:45.344
it's ludicrous.

00:28:50.858 --> 00:28:51.984
What's this?

00:28:54.295 --> 00:28:56.320
The tremor must have
shaken the rocks loose.

00:28:56.364 --> 00:28:57.626
Well, they're in the way.

00:28:57.665 --> 00:28:58.689
No, hold it.

00:28:58.733 --> 00:29:00.325
We don't know how
stable this tunnel is.

00:29:00.368 --> 00:29:02.802
An energy blast might bring the
rest of it down on our heads.

00:29:02.837 --> 00:29:03.895
Let go!

00:29:04.005 --> 00:29:05.734
No.

00:29:05.773 --> 00:29:07.468
I think I should keep this.

00:29:09.944 --> 00:29:12.674
Never pick a fight
with a Klingon, Tom.

00:29:12.714 --> 00:29:14.204
I'm not going to fight
with you, B'Elanna.

00:29:14.248 --> 00:29:15.237
Afraid I'll break your arm?

00:29:15.283 --> 00:29:16.272
You should be.

00:29:18.486 --> 00:29:20.386
B'Elanna, stop it!

00:29:20.421 --> 00:29:21.911
This isn't about the gun.

00:29:22.023 --> 00:29:23.183
This is about sex.

00:29:23.224 --> 00:29:26.125
But that's not going
to happen right now.

00:29:27.295 --> 00:29:28.785
I think it is.

00:29:30.531 --> 00:29:32.590
See, I've picked up
your scent, Tom.

00:29:32.634 --> 00:29:33.896
I've tasted your blood.

00:29:35.603 --> 00:29:37.093
No.

00:29:37.138 --> 00:29:40.107
No, I'm your friend

00:29:40.141 --> 00:29:41.472
and I have to watch out for you

00:29:41.509 --> 00:29:43.033
when your judgment's
been impaired.

00:29:43.077 --> 00:29:45.511
If you let these instincts
take over now,

00:29:45.546 --> 00:29:46.774
you'll hate yourself

00:29:46.814 --> 00:29:49.305
and me, too,
for taking advantage of you.

00:29:52.186 --> 00:29:53.813
I won't do that.

00:30:02.263 --> 00:30:03.252
Maybe...

00:30:04.899 --> 00:30:06.924
maybe we should
continue separately.

00:30:06.968 --> 00:30:07.935
No.

00:30:07.969 --> 00:30:10.699
You don't know how strong...

00:30:10.738 --> 00:30:14.868
how hard it is to fight this...

00:30:14.909 --> 00:30:16.604
urge.

00:30:16.644 --> 00:30:18.976
Are you telling me
that I'm impossible to resist?

00:30:19.981 --> 00:30:21.881
I wouldn't go that far.

00:30:23.084 --> 00:30:24.551
Good.

00:30:26.554 --> 00:30:27.885
Come on.

00:30:40.435 --> 00:30:43.165
I want to know about the vessel
which brought you here...

00:30:43.204 --> 00:30:47.368
your propulsion systems,
weapons, sensors... everything.

00:30:49.510 --> 00:30:52.536
You have an artificial implant
in your arm.

00:30:52.580 --> 00:30:55.777
Yes. It was necessary
to replace the elbow joint

00:30:55.817 --> 00:30:58.149
after I was injured
in a combat simulation.

00:30:59.587 --> 00:31:02.385
I also want to know
about your medical technology...

00:31:02.423 --> 00:31:06.416
scientific advances,
artificial intelligence...

00:31:06.461 --> 00:31:08.088
I'd be glad to tell you
all about my people

00:31:08.129 --> 00:31:09.118
and learn about yours.

00:31:09.163 --> 00:31:11.324
There's no need to hold us
here for interrogation.

00:31:11.365 --> 00:31:13.128
You should expect
no better treatment

00:31:13.167 --> 00:31:14.725
after invading Sakari territory.

00:31:14.769 --> 00:31:17.795
As I said, we didn't know
there was anyone down here.

00:31:17.839 --> 00:31:19.932
Yes... so you've said.

00:31:19.974 --> 00:31:21.373
Your people have clearly made

00:31:21.409 --> 00:31:23.570
every effort to avoid
detection by outsiders.

00:31:23.611 --> 00:31:24.908
Is it so difficult to believe

00:31:24.946 --> 00:31:27.107
that those measures were
effective in our case?

00:31:27.148 --> 00:31:28.945
If they had been fully
effective, you wouldn't

00:31:28.983 --> 00:31:31.417
have found anything interesting
enough to bring you here.

00:31:31.452 --> 00:31:33.079
That's something
we can help you with.

00:31:33.121 --> 00:31:34.986
What?

00:31:35.056 --> 00:31:36.580
We can show you
how we detected the gallicite,

00:31:36.624 --> 00:31:38.819
so you can disguise it better.

00:31:38.860 --> 00:31:40.259
We can also help you eliminate

00:31:40.294 --> 00:31:42.353
the last traces
of the ruins on the surface,

00:31:42.396 --> 00:31:44.387
so no one else
will be curious about them.

00:31:44.432 --> 00:31:45.763
You've seen the ruins?

00:31:45.800 --> 00:31:46.767
Yes.

00:31:46.801 --> 00:31:48.666
I assume the Sakari
once lived there.

00:31:48.703 --> 00:31:50.762
Long ago...

00:31:50.805 --> 00:31:52.272
before I was born.

00:31:52.306 --> 00:31:53.603
What happened?

00:31:53.641 --> 00:31:56.872
My people never even knew
who the invaders were

00:31:56.911 --> 00:31:58.401
or why they attacked.

00:31:58.446 --> 00:32:00.209
It was all over
in less than an hour.

00:32:00.248 --> 00:32:02.512
Some of the colonists
were fortunate enough

00:32:02.550 --> 00:32:04.313
to escape into the mines.

00:32:04.352 --> 00:32:08.948
We've lived here ever
since, where it's safe.

00:32:09.056 --> 00:32:11.217
If the invaders ever learned
of our existence here,

00:32:11.259 --> 00:32:12.692
they might return.

00:32:12.727 --> 00:32:14.922
I certainly understand
your caution,

00:32:14.962 --> 00:32:16.725
but let us demonstrate
our good faith

00:32:16.764 --> 00:32:18.425
by helping you
protect yourselves.

00:32:18.466 --> 00:32:21.264
Then we'll go
and never bother you again.

00:32:27.074 --> 00:32:28.939
Agreed.

00:32:28.976 --> 00:32:31.536
But you will be supervised
at all times.

00:32:38.653 --> 00:32:40.086
We're almost
to the next passageway.

00:32:40.121 --> 00:32:41.088
Can you make it?

00:32:41.122 --> 00:32:42.749
Not much choice.

00:33:02.977 --> 00:33:04.501
It's all right.

00:33:04.545 --> 00:33:06.740
We'll find a way out.

00:33:06.781 --> 00:33:08.146
We should use that weapon.

00:33:08.182 --> 00:33:09.444
It's worth the risk now.

00:33:09.483 --> 00:33:11.951
Well, I might agree with you
if I still had it.

00:33:11.986 --> 00:33:14.284
It's buried somewhere
under all that.

00:33:14.322 --> 00:33:15.289
What?!

00:33:15.323 --> 00:33:16.620
Sorry.

00:33:20.228 --> 00:33:21.718
Try to stay calm.

00:33:21.762 --> 00:33:23.252
I know it's hard.

00:33:23.297 --> 00:33:24.958
You don't know anything!

00:33:25.032 --> 00:33:26.966
I feel like I'm crawling
out of my skin!

00:33:27.034 --> 00:33:28.467
I need to do something.

00:33:28.502 --> 00:33:29.628
I can't take this!

00:33:40.882 --> 00:33:43.373
You've never been
hard to get, Tom.

00:33:43.417 --> 00:33:45.908
Well, I'm making an exception.

00:33:45.953 --> 00:33:47.477
I can't let you do this.

00:33:47.521 --> 00:33:48.488
Oh?

00:33:48.522 --> 00:33:50.114
Oh, but you wish you could.

00:33:50.157 --> 00:33:53.126
All those invitations
to dinner...

00:33:53.160 --> 00:33:56.288
and on the holodeck,
the way you would stare at me

00:33:56.330 --> 00:33:58.628
when you thought
I wasn't looking...

00:33:58.666 --> 00:34:01.760
and get jealous
when I'm with someone else.

00:34:01.802 --> 00:34:06.205
You can't tell me you're
not interested in me.

00:34:08.709 --> 00:34:10.609
You're right.

00:34:10.645 --> 00:34:12.840
I can't.

00:34:12.880 --> 00:34:16.475
Then don't push me away.

00:34:17.685 --> 00:34:19.778
Oh, believe me, I'd like to,

00:34:19.820 --> 00:34:23.517
but I know
this isn't really you.

00:34:23.557 --> 00:34:26.822
You've made it clear
that you're not interested

00:34:26.861 --> 00:34:29.295
and I have to accept
that's how you feel, even now.

00:34:32.733 --> 00:34:34.963
No...

00:34:35.069 --> 00:34:36.764
no, it isn't.

00:34:39.040 --> 00:34:41.474
I was... I was just
afraid to admit it.

00:34:43.577 --> 00:34:46.011
You see, I've wanted
this for so long.

00:34:52.086 --> 00:34:53.815
Just let it happen.

00:35:16.844 --> 00:35:19.506
I hope someday you'll say
that to me and mean it.

00:35:21.983 --> 00:35:24.645
You'd let me go insane
rather than help me?!

00:35:24.685 --> 00:35:26.084
You know that's not true.

00:35:26.120 --> 00:35:29.248
You just...
stay away from me!

00:35:52.446 --> 00:35:53.538
You called, Ensign?

00:35:53.581 --> 00:35:55.845
Is there a... problem?

00:35:55.883 --> 00:35:57.214
Not at all.

00:35:57.251 --> 00:35:59.219
You seem...

00:35:59.253 --> 00:36:00.720
much improved.

00:36:00.755 --> 00:36:01.722
Yes.

00:36:01.756 --> 00:36:04.554
Your holodeck therapy
was very effective.

00:36:04.592 --> 00:36:07.891
I must compliment you
on an innovative solution.

00:36:07.928 --> 00:36:09.896
I'm pleased to hear that.

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:12.160
This could be
a viable alternative

00:36:12.199 --> 00:36:13.894
for space-faring Vulcans.

00:36:13.934 --> 00:36:17.301
When we get back, I'm sure
Starfleet medical will...

00:36:17.338 --> 00:36:20.398
never hear about your
personal experiences from me.

00:36:20.441 --> 00:36:21.567
Thank you, Doctor.

00:36:21.609 --> 00:36:24.635
May I return to duty?

00:36:24.678 --> 00:36:25.702
Soon enough, Ensign.

00:36:25.746 --> 00:36:27.907
I'll need to run
a few more cortical scans.

00:36:27.948 --> 00:36:30.576
Mr. Vorik's biochemical
readings are stabilizing.

00:36:30.618 --> 00:36:32.813
They're not back to normal yet,

00:36:32.853 --> 00:36:35.151
but I believe he's gotten
through the worst of it.

00:36:35.189 --> 00:36:36.816
I'm ready to release him
from Sick Bay.

00:36:36.857 --> 00:36:37.824
Good work, Doctor.

00:36:37.858 --> 00:36:39.450
Will this treatment
help B'Elanna as well?

00:36:39.493 --> 00:36:40.551
I don't see why not.

00:36:40.594 --> 00:36:41.856
As soon as the away
team gets back,

00:36:41.896 --> 00:36:42.954
I'll send her straight to you.

00:36:43.064 --> 00:36:44.190
I'll get to work designing

00:36:44.231 --> 00:36:46.096
the half-Klingon version
of the program.

00:36:46.133 --> 00:36:47.760
There's a copious
amount of information

00:36:47.802 --> 00:36:50.965
in the cultural database
about their mating practices.

00:36:51.072 --> 00:36:53.632
Did you know
that fracturing a clavicle

00:36:53.674 --> 00:36:55.767
on the wedding night
is actually

00:36:55.810 --> 00:36:57.971
considered a blessing
on the marriage?

00:36:58.079 --> 00:36:59.876
As a matter of fact, I didn't.

00:36:59.914 --> 00:37:01.779
I'm planning to do
a comparative study

00:37:01.816 --> 00:37:03.306
of all these mating rituals.

00:37:03.350 --> 00:37:04.817
It really is fascinating...

00:37:06.454 --> 00:37:08.854
...from a sociobiological
point of view.

00:37:08.889 --> 00:37:12.120
I'm sure B'Elanna will
appreciate your efforts, Doctor.

00:37:19.165 --> 00:37:21.099
Mm.

00:37:29.708 --> 00:37:31.175
Where are we?

00:37:31.210 --> 00:37:33.770
Still stuck in the cave,
I'm afraid.

00:37:33.813 --> 00:37:35.678
The caves?

00:37:35.714 --> 00:37:38.239
The gallicite...
where's my tricorder?

00:37:38.284 --> 00:37:41.776
No, we're not looking
for the gallicite anymore.

00:37:41.821 --> 00:37:43.982
We're trying to get back
to the ship, remember?

00:37:46.525 --> 00:37:49.961
No... I don't.

00:37:59.438 --> 00:38:01.338
Are you two all right?

00:38:01.373 --> 00:38:02.863
B'Elanna needs help.

00:38:02.908 --> 00:38:04.603
We've got to get her
out of here.

00:38:18.457 --> 00:38:20.254
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:38:20.292 --> 00:38:22.920
Please respond.

00:38:22.995 --> 00:38:25.395
Still nothing.

00:38:25.431 --> 00:38:27.296
What's the matter?

00:38:27.333 --> 00:38:28.630
Why aren't they answering?

00:38:28.667 --> 00:38:30.692
There must be some kind
of communications problem.

00:38:30.736 --> 00:38:32.294
I'm sure they'll
clear it up soon.

00:38:32.338 --> 00:38:33.566
It may not be soon enough.

00:38:33.606 --> 00:38:36.632
I am concerned about the rapid
progression of her symptoms.

00:38:36.675 --> 00:38:39.405
You must help her now,
Mr. Paris.

00:38:39.445 --> 00:38:43.040
If she does not resolve
the Pon farr,

00:38:43.082 --> 00:38:45.073
she will die.

00:38:56.295 --> 00:39:00.925
B'Elanna, I know this is
a pretty bizarre situation...

00:39:00.966 --> 00:39:03.127
probably not what either
one of us had in mind...

00:39:03.168 --> 00:39:05.796
but it's too late
to worry about that now.

00:39:05.838 --> 00:39:07.100
Tom...

00:39:07.139 --> 00:39:08.800
What?

00:39:08.841 --> 00:39:10.399
Be quiet.

00:39:19.752 --> 00:39:22.312
So, this is the part

00:39:22.354 --> 00:39:24.549
where you throw
heavy objects at me?

00:39:24.590 --> 00:39:26.785
Maybe later.

00:39:30.329 --> 00:39:33.856
I'm not sure exactly
what I'm supposed to do.

00:39:48.581 --> 00:39:50.549
Well, what are you doing?

00:39:50.583 --> 00:39:53.108
Enjoying myself?

00:39:53.152 --> 00:39:54.619
Then show it.

00:40:04.897 --> 00:40:09.061
You are my mate, not his!

00:40:09.101 --> 00:40:10.295
What are you doing here?

00:40:10.336 --> 00:40:12.463
I've come to claim you,
to fulfill our bond

00:40:12.504 --> 00:40:15.496
and if necessary,
to face my rival!

00:40:15.541 --> 00:40:16.803
Lieutenant Tuvok!

00:40:20.646 --> 00:40:21.977
Ensign.

00:40:22.081 --> 00:40:27.178
Sir, I declare
Koon-ut kal-if-fee.

00:40:27.219 --> 00:40:28.208
The ritual challenge.

00:40:28.253 --> 00:40:29.982
He intends to fight
to win his mate.

00:40:30.022 --> 00:40:31.546
If you want a fight,
you've got one.

00:40:31.590 --> 00:40:32.557
Hold on, Tom.

00:40:32.591 --> 00:40:34.582
There's not going
to be any challenge.

00:40:34.627 --> 00:40:37.425
Are you responsible for the ship
being out of contact?

00:40:37.463 --> 00:40:40.728
It was necessary
to disable the communications,

00:40:40.766 --> 00:40:42.199
transporters and shuttles.

00:40:42.234 --> 00:40:44.202
No one will keep me
from my mate!

00:40:44.236 --> 00:40:46.670
I am not your mate!

00:40:46.705 --> 00:40:48.229
We will soon decide that!

00:40:48.273 --> 00:40:49.240
If anyone is going to smash

00:40:49.274 --> 00:40:51.139
your arrogant little face in,
I will!

00:40:51.176 --> 00:40:53.736
I take your challenge myself!

00:40:53.779 --> 00:40:56.748
She has the right
to choose her own defender...

00:40:56.782 --> 00:40:57.840
even herself.

00:40:57.883 --> 00:40:59.373
Now, just hold on.

00:40:59.418 --> 00:41:01.283
Neither of you are thinking
straight right now.

00:41:01.320 --> 00:41:02.912
They are following
their instincts

00:41:02.955 --> 00:41:04.946
and I suggest
we allow them to do so.

00:41:05.057 --> 00:41:06.217
You mean, let them fight?

00:41:06.258 --> 00:41:07.589
It is logical.

00:41:07.626 --> 00:41:10.356
Both must resolve their Pon farr
before it kills them.

00:41:10.396 --> 00:41:12.193
We cannot wait
to hear from Voyager.

00:41:12.231 --> 00:41:13.789
They'll tear each other
to pieces!

00:41:13.832 --> 00:41:15.424
The risk of injury
seems preferable

00:41:15.467 --> 00:41:18.163
to the certainty of dying
from a chemical imbalance.

00:41:18.203 --> 00:41:22.765
Commander, I see no alternative
but to follow Vulcan tradition.

00:41:28.313 --> 00:41:29.974
All right.

00:41:30.015 --> 00:41:31.312
Begin.

00:42:43.455 --> 00:42:45.389
It's over, isn't it?

00:42:45.424 --> 00:42:47.187
The blood fever has been purged.

00:42:47.226 --> 00:42:48.887
They will both recover.

00:42:52.965 --> 00:42:56.867
Captain's Log, Stardate 50541.6.

00:42:56.902 --> 00:42:58.870
We're following through
with Chakotay's offer

00:42:58.904 --> 00:43:01.634
to help the Sakari
improve their camouflage,

00:43:01.673 --> 00:43:02.867
and they've agreed to supply us

00:43:02.908 --> 00:43:05.172
with a generous quantity
of gallicite.

00:43:13.819 --> 00:43:15.013
Deck 2.

00:43:19.925 --> 00:43:23.122
So, looks like
you're feeling better.

00:43:23.162 --> 00:43:24.561
Hmm.

00:43:24.596 --> 00:43:25.585
You back on duty?

00:43:25.631 --> 00:43:26.791
- Yes.
- Hmm.

00:43:26.832 --> 00:43:29.665
Yes, I'm fine.
Thanks.

00:43:31.370 --> 00:43:33.270
The refit is going well.

00:43:33.305 --> 00:43:35.773
We should have new warp coils
by the end of the week.

00:43:35.808 --> 00:43:36.775
Oh, good.

00:43:36.809 --> 00:43:37.935
Glad to hear it.

00:43:40.946 --> 00:43:42.971
Computer, halt turbolift.

00:43:43.048 --> 00:43:45.346
Look, this is ridiculous.

00:43:45.384 --> 00:43:47.545
We are going to be together
on this ship for a long time.

00:43:47.586 --> 00:43:48.746
You're right.

00:43:48.787 --> 00:43:51.517
We have to pretend that the
whole mission didn't happen.

00:43:51.557 --> 00:43:53.684
But something did happen,
B'Elanna.

00:43:53.725 --> 00:43:56.285
Look, Tom, I really
appreciate what you did...

00:43:56.328 --> 00:43:58.660
what you were willing
to do for me...

00:43:58.697 --> 00:44:01.461
but as far as I'm concerned,
I was under the influence

00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:03.491
of some weird Vulcan
chemical imbalance

00:44:03.535 --> 00:44:08.802
and whatever I did, whatever
I said... it wasn't me.

00:44:08.841 --> 00:44:10.809
Yeah, I know.

00:44:10.843 --> 00:44:14.574
You're afraid that
your big, scary Klingon side

00:44:14.613 --> 00:44:16.376
might have been showing.

00:44:16.415 --> 00:44:18.178
Well, I saw it up close

00:44:18.217 --> 00:44:21.186
and you know,
it wasn't so terrible.

00:44:21.220 --> 00:44:24.212
In fact, I wouldn't mind
seeing it again someday.

00:44:31.763 --> 00:44:35.221
Computer... resume.

00:44:40.672 --> 00:44:42.799
Careful what you wish for,
Lieutenant.

00:44:45.444 --> 00:44:46.502
Your call sounded urgent.

00:44:46.545 --> 00:44:48.638
I think there's something
you should see, Captain.

00:44:48.680 --> 00:44:50.978
We found this as we were
clearing away the ruins.

00:44:51.016 --> 00:44:55.180
Undoubtedly, one of the invaders
who destroyed this colony.

00:44:55.220 --> 00:44:57.484
The Borg.
